  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA-2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 accuracy, a large jump over config_001 (single-profile, 0.485), confirming that multi-profile aggregation is the most impactful design choice so far. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the gain comes primarily from having multiple profiles or from the aggregation method itself—specifically, whether a transformer aggregator can further improve over simple average pooling. This experiment (config_003) changes exactly one variable from config_002 (avgpool → transformer) while holding encoder, profile setting, and modality fixed, giving a clean A/B comparison. If transformer significantly outperforms avgpool, it justifies the added complexity in all downstream multimodal experiments; if it does not, avgpool is confirmed as sufficient and we can rule out transformer across the remaining search space, saving budget. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice because it directly extends the strongest result with a single-variable change."
}

